/-!
# Selection and action transport for the field-four triangle

Both quotient orientations supply the literal third vertex's source
hypotheses and a chosen Irr⁺ module. The kernel on its Sylow join is
computed directly. Fixed-space vanishing from the full earlier shadow
implication lifts natural quotient coordinates to the whole module.
Geometric radical representatives then construct its actual action on
that module, and the original-flag consumer produces a mutually
normalizing conjugate with action rank at least four.

The preceding normalized 7.0.1 and 3.2.5 conclusions now recognize the same
chosen module in both orientations, preserving its central quotient and
constructing its natural field-four action. The compatible paired flags
now have both orientation-specific contradiction applications. The selected
module has a constructed invariant flag, and rank-one covering identifies
its first residual with K₀. Containment of the original Cartan in the new
vertex makes it a Cartan there; its orbit forces K to centralize the new point.
The common second residual is now identified in both orientations. Mutual
normalizer escape follows from its nonsolvability and local maximality,
completing triangle exclusion without additional component placement or
generation hypotheses. The exact surviving refinement follows from the
preceding complete 11.1.2 alternatives. Earlier source inputs retain their
final discharge with the parent component assembly.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith 11.1.2(3), pp.762--764, and 11.4.1(2), p.776.
-/
